ng_ubt: set the isochronous alternate setting by voice link

ng_ubt set interface 1 once, at attach, to the alternate setting with
the largest wMaxPacketSize. The controller sizes its isochronous SCO
stream by the setting the host chose for the links it carries (Core
Vol 4 Part B 2.1.1), so with one CVSD link at alt 5 the host's SCO
packets are out of step with the controller's and headset audio is
garbage or silent; mSBC wide-band speech needs alt 1 (or 6).

- Follow the controller's synchronous links in the events ng_ubt carries
  up (Connection_Complete for SCO, Synchronous_Connection_Complete,
  Disconnection_Complete) and the voice setting in the commands it
  carries down, and pick the setting as the transport spec and other
  stacks do: alt 2/4/5 for 1-3 CVSD links with 16-bit input (1/2/3 for
  8-bit), alt 6 or else 1 for a transparent link, the attach setting
  with no link. ng_ubt_sco.c (this directory's src/) keeps that state in
  a side table, so struct ubt_softc keeps its layout.
- Apply it from the USB explore process, as uaudio does: stop the
  isochronous transfers, change the setting, set them up again for the
  new packet size and restart them (ubt_isoc_set_alt()). ubt_detach()
  waits for a change in flight.
- NGM_UBT_NODE_SET_ISOC_ALT / GET_ISOC_ALT ("set_isoc_alt",
  "get_isoc_alt", ng_ubt_sco.h) force a setting or report the state;
  net.bluetooth.usb_isoc_auto_alt=0 turns the automatic choice off.

Origin: NextBSD (nextbsd/nextbsd-kernel#237). Not upstream.
Applies to: releng/15.1 sys/netgraph/bluetooth/drivers/ubt/ng_ubt.c

